# fixedbugs, defect 2516, lane b35-link, 2026-11-13.
#
# SYMPTOM: `twice`, which this module's header calls from the body of the
# function its group binds and another module's header only declares:
# refused with *the two headers' own code calls* it, half false.
#
# FIX: the note says what the compiler knows, that neither module's C calls
# `twice` through a group and that a header's own code is where C reaches
# it; here this header's does, through `long long`, while the other's says
# `double`.
use fixedbugs2516/declares_b

extern "fixedbugs-2516-calls-a.h"  #~ ffi_declared_two_ways
    function calls_a_value(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(calls_a_value(x: 3))
    print(declares_b.b(x: 3))
